{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And to me, your thoughts</b> — מחשבותיך (your thoughts) corresponding to בנת לרעי (I considered my companion). The meaning: for You know all my thoughts, but I do not know Your thoughts, for they are too lofty for me, and precious is the knowledge of them. The meaning of יקרים is a thing of scarcity, as in ויקר פדיון נפשם (Psalm 49:8). And if the thought is one, the actions that follow from it are many; therefore he said מה עצמו ראשיהם (how mighty is their sum). The meaning: the sum of Your thoughts."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {0 "Resolved יקרים as 'precious' from context; the quoted phrase ויקר פדיון נפשם supports his lexical argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:13.766264898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}